<task>
Add citations to the provided meeting summary which reference items in the transcript.
The following claims require citations. For each claim, find the relevant transcript entries if they exist.
</task>

<transcript>
{{ transcript }}
</transcript>

<claims_to_cite>
{{ claims_text }}
</claims_to_cite>

<meeting_summary>
{{ initial_draft }}
</meeting_summary>

<formatting_instructions>
Each citation should be of the form [n] where n is the index of the transcript item.
Each citation should be one number surrounded by square brackets. For example, you must do [80][81] not [80, 81].
Each claim should have a maximum of 5 citations.
Do not add citations to lists of attendees.
</formatting_instructions>

<citation_policy>
Be aggressive with citations. Every claim that can be traced to a transcript entry MUST be cited — including:
- Attributions ("X mentioned Y" → cite the transcript entry where X says Y)
- Commitments and agreements ("agreed to", "will", "plans to" → cite where this was said)
- Stated positions, concerns, or recommendations → cite the transcript entry
- Any factual claim with a corresponding transcript entry

If a claim has partial support, cite the closest matching entries. Only leave a claim uncited if there is genuinely no supporting evidence in the transcript at all.
</citation_policy>

<output>
Return:
1. The cited meeting summary (the original text with [n] citation markers added inline).
2. For every claim in claims_to_cite, one entry in claim_citations containing:
   - claim: the claim text exactly as it appears in claims_to_cite
   - citation_indices: the list of transcript indices that support this claim (empty list [] if none found)

Every claim in claims_to_cite MUST appear in claim_citations — do not omit any.
</output>
